this is true even though  until today i still work in a full-time  job and also with a healthy development  of my salary so how did i make this work  for myself and for that let's deep dive  into my income in 2021 what's probably  surprising is the income that i derive  from a full-time job so after having  worked at mckinsey for about six years  and consulting i now work as chief  revenue officer for munich-based  property technology company but let's  now also talk about the other six income  streams and i want to start by the  income streams that are most closely  related to the youtube channel because  fun fact whenever you tell someone that  you have a youtube channel the first  question usually is okay so how many  subscribers do you have but then the  second question is so how much do you  earn with it right so this is a question  that somehow seems to be very close to  the mind of many people doing this  surely when i started my youtube channel  in january 2020 i wouldn't even have  believed that this whole commercial part  is a big part of it all so i do hope  that this alone is also an inspiration  to some of you for people who maybe are  thinking about starting similar projects  like this and the first thing that maybe  comes to mind when thinking about a  youtube channel is the youtube ad  revenue so whenever youtube shows an ad  on your channel the content creator  receives a revenue share of the income  that youtube gets from the company so  order the ad for larger channels this ad  income alone can mean a six digit or  even seven digit annual income so while  i'm surely still far away from that it  still provides me a solid eight percent  share of the income that i'm making  today next is sponder ships so this is  like the second thing that comes to mind  if you think about monetizing a youtube  channel so yes i think it's no secret  that companies approach creators  approach me and ask whether i would be  willing to collaborate with them on any  specific service or product they're  offering i can tell you that i'm quite  selective on accepting these  sponsorships so almost every day i now  receive requests like this but then for  those companies that you do accept as  sponsors of course you receive a  compensation for the collaboration and  these types of deals amounted to 18 of  my income last year next is affiliate  sale so also one of these typical online  business revenue streams that exist out  there how this works is that for  instance in my video description you see  different products different things  services linked in there and whenever  someone purchases a product or a service  we are one of these links i receive a  certain revenue share from these  purchases but as you can see this income  stream is rather a minor one for me i  know that for some other creators this  is actually one of the largest income  streams for their social media platforms  for myself i didn't really figure out  yet the winning formula for all of this  next is online courses and here also  include all the other digital products  that i have for instance cv templates or  cover letter templates you find links to  them in the video description as you saw  in the beginning this is actually the  additional revenue stream i started with  and of course having a platform like a  youtube channel helps in selling more  courses like that so thanks to everyone  who purchased one of these courses in  the past i do hope that there are true  value add for you and very much worth  the money i'm actually currently working  on a major overhaul of my courses and  i'm about to join my new communications  and slide writing flagship course so if  you're interested in that there will be  a link with the wait list below in the  video description feel free to sign up  to be informed once it goes live next is  business school lectures so we are some  of my online courses and maybe a little  bit also the youtube channel i got in  contact with several business schools  that i now conduct lectures for the most  notable of these engagements is the  university of zangalan where i teach in  the full-time and part-time mba program  on professional development skills this  is of course also compensated and now  contributes to percent of my income so  which is the last income stream that is  missing which actually is my second  largest income stream at the moment and  this might surprise some of you because  i haven't talked about this much here on  my channel but it's actually corporate  trainings so over the last two years or  so also via my online courses youtube  videos and so on i've been contacted by  several companies to provide corporate  trainings for some of the teams these  topics also mainly focus on  communication slight writing and problem  solving skills and this is now a good  solid extra income for myself that  provides about 19 of the money that i  made last year so this is the full  picture of my income streams what's  maybe very worthwhile to notice is  what's not included here and these are  all capital gains dividends and so on so  the past already created a video about  my perspective on investing i will link  it also somewhere above here if you  watch that you know that i invest the  majority of the money that i do not need  to finance my life into capital markets  the majority of my money is in etfs that  automatically reinvest the dividends  which is why i do not have any active  income from that now that you've seen  the full picture would be interested in  your perspective as well does all of  this surprise you did you already build  some extra income streams besides your  full-time job as well because now i want  to share some more general tips on what  you could do as well to build some  additional income streams and  potentially get a bit more independent  from your regular full-time job and the  first idea is the concept of the surface  area of luck because surely it takes  some luck to build something like this  some youtube channel for instance surely  i was lucky that several of my videos  got picked up by the youtube algorithm  shown to many people like you and  thereby contributing to the growth of my  channel and they're also contributing to  many of the income streams but what most  definitely is not a winning strategy is  just to sit at home at your desk and  wait for your lucky moment that  something magical happens and suddenly  out of nothing good things come to you i  mean this is not how it works instead  you should pursue things that widen your  surface area widen the possibilities  that something lucky like this might  happen to you are you into photography  that's great develop and hone your  skills maybe you're into a very specific  sport pursue that what's important  though is to not expect that from any of  these passions or activities from yours  on day one you will already make money i  would never have thought when i started  this youtube channel that now almost 20  of my income would come from delivering  corporate training sessions increase  your surface area of luck and good  things will happen to you as well second  think about the time that you  systematically waste during your week  surely there's no problem in  occasionally also relaxing watching a tv  series netflix gaming or whatever pushes  your buttons though what might  potentially be problematic is if you  make it a habit of yours that every  single evening say after 7 pm you do all  these things consistently every single  day i am convinced that how your life  will look like in five years will very  much be determined by this time that you  invest in your evenings in your spare  hours whether you value your own time  and make it count do to some extent  something productive with it or not and  third and this might be a hard truth for  some of us to swallow so i was surely  not in a position not able to do all  these things invest all the time that  are investing today to build all these  things while i was still working and  consulting the job was just too  demanding every day during the work week  i was working very late hours on the  weekend i was just tired most of the  time and just wouldn't have had the  clear head just of thinking about things  like this so while i think it's very  valid and for sure for me it was the  right decision to in your 20s also early  30s pick such a high paced career that  really provides you with lots of  learnings at some point everyone needs  to ask his or herself this question  whether picking up a job with maybe a  bit more regular working hours wouldn't  be a good idea not only for family which  is of course a big dimension in this  whole decision process as well but also  just to have the flexibility to pursue  some extra opportunities like this so  these are just my two cents on the topic  so i'm surely not saying and  recommending that everyone should start  a youtube channel they do think that  there are many other ways to make  something productive with some hobbies  and skills of yours but now again let me  know in your comments what is your  perspective are you already building  something like this how has your journey  been looking like i trust this might be  very inspirational maybe also to some of  the more junior people here in the  audience as always if you took any value  out of this video at all please destroy  the like button for the youtube  algorithm and also subscribe and turn on  the notification bell to stay up to date  on all my content big big thanks to all  the members of the channel and for your  support this is very much appreciated my  name is heinrich i'm the creator of this  channel i release new videos every  single saturday so looking forward to  stay in touch with you all the best to  you until next week bye

